To compare the numbers $13.17$ and $13.7$, we align them by their decimal points:

$$
\begin{array}{r@{\quad}l}
  13.17 \\
  13.70 & \text{(adding a trailing zero for comparison)}
\end{array}
$$

Now, compare the digits from left to right after the decimal point:
- The tenths place: $1$ vs $7$. Since $7 > 1$, the number with $7$ in the tenths place is larger.

Therefore, $13.7$ is larger than $13.17$.

\boxed{13.7}
